diff --git a/docs/P2P_BACKEND_RECONCILIATION.md b/docs/P2P_BACKEND_RECONCILIATION.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..c879c4c2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/P2P_BACKEND_RECONCILIATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+# P2P backend release source and verification
+
+The runnable backend in this workspace is `artifacts/p2p-app-backend`.
+Its routes, models and dependency manifest are the source for backend deployment.
+The similarly named subtree in the Flutter repository is an incomplete
+integration snapshot, not a standalone server. Do not deploy that subtree or
+the older `bazz-backend-02` checkout as a shortcut.
+
+## Reconciled contracts
+
+- `POST /api/v1/iap/verify` accepts authenticated users and trainers.
+  Standard/Pro quarterly/annual IDs and legacy monthly/annual restores share
+  a server catalog. Apple/Google are authoritative; cached active rows do not
+  bypass store verification. Purchase and profile writes are transactional.
+- Restoring a store subscription does not erase a customer's human trainer.
+  Original transaction ownership cannot move between accounts.
+- Legacy affiliate behavior is preserved for initial legacy activations only;
+  restoring does not credit twice. No prices are invented for new products.
+- `GET /api/v1/enterprise/me/context` aliases the existing bootstrap.
+  `PUT` saves a server-validated gym/location preference. Bootstrap restores it
+  and rechecks database membership. `tenantId: null` explicitly selects personal
+  mode. A revoked preference does not silently select another gym.
+- Live registry records may carry approved branding and locations. Existing
+  records remain compatible. Unknown gyms fall back to neutral colors, and
+  KMF's bundled fallback is green. Existing configured palettes override defaults.
+
+## Backend release preparation
+
+```
+node scripts/prepare-p2p-backend-release.mjs
+```
+
+This compiles the complete backend into a new generated directory and creates
+an archive containing compiled code, source, package manifest and SHA-256 source
+inventory. It excludes credentials, databases, node_modules, media and tests.
+It never deploys. Its manifest distinguishes the workspace checkpoint from the
+actual included source hashes; a checkpoint ID alone does not attest uncommitted files.
+
+## Verification
+
+```
+pnpm --filter @workspace/p2p-app-backend run build
+pnpm --filter @workspace/p2p-app-backend exec jest --runInBand \
+  src/__tests__/iap-security.test.ts \
+  src/__tests__/enterprise-compatibility.test.ts
+node --test scripts/tests/p2p_iap_persistence.cjs
+```
+
+The persistence suite starts a separate temporary Mongo replica set, uses fake
+store responses, and tears it down. It never uses the development/production
+database and never charges a card or store account.
+
+The installed Jest launcher currently points to a missing package, so those
+Jest checks cannot run in this workspace without repairing its test dependencies.
+The native Node persistence suite independently exercises the compiled service,
+real Mongo transactions, real signed test JWTs, and the gym bootstrap/selection
+controllers. Do not report the Jest suites or Flutter tests as passed.
+
+Mongo transactions require a replica set. The workspace's standalone mongod
+cannot execute transactional purchase activations; it must fail closed rather
+than granting access with partial writes. Production Atlas supports transactions.
+
+## Still required before claiming launch readiness
+
+Configure deployment store credentials; deploy the reviewed backend with approval;
+verify lifecycle notifications, refund/cancellation handling and sandbox purchases;
+complete gym-scoped trainer/booking checks; run Flutter analysis and physical-device
+QA; restore Codemagic access; build/sign/upload to TestFlight and confirm processing.
+Neither a passing compilation nor this archive is proof of those steps.
diff --git a/scripts/prepare-p2p-backend-release.mjs b/scripts/prepare-p2p-backend-release.mjs
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..527f2d6b
